SCOPE / PATH NOTE (documented — no silent drift)
------------------------------------------------------------
The web source `components/ui/Typography.tsx` is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL primitive library
(Heading / Text + 11 convenience roles) driven by @/lib/tokens `typography.role`. It has no
data sources, no t() calls, and no conditional render branches.

The atomic typography PRIMITIVES are already ported to
  apps/apple/Sources/Components/UI/Typography.swift
  (TSPageTitle, TSSectionTitle, TSText, TSCaption, TSLabel, TSMetricValue, TSCode, ...)
and the prompt explicitly places "Atomic shared components" OUT OF SCOPE ("covered by the P4
component-library bundle prompt"). This surface therefore does NOT re-declare those primitives.

This shared SURFACE is delivered as the native type-specimen / showcase surface
(`TypographyShowcase`) that reproduces every web `typography.role` (page/section/panel titles,
subhead, body, captions, label, metric value/label, code, helper, error) at its true
size / weight / tracking / colour / case, grouped into specimen sections — meaningful
cross-feature design-system chrome (the "Shared surface" tier). It consumes the P1/S9 tokens
(Font.TS / Color.TS / TSTypeMetrics / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMaterial) exactly as the existing
AiUsageCard surface does (Text(verbatim:) + tokens), so the specimen can never drift from the
role identities.

