PARITY (web source reproduced)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Roles: all 13 web `typography.role` entries decomposed into native metric specs (point size,
  weight, tracking, semantic colour, uppercase / monospaced / tabular-figures traits), modelled as
  a data table (the native port of the web `typography.role` object). pageTitle / metricValue use
  the largest responsive step (30 pt) = Font.TS.display; tracking-tight = TSTypeMetrics tracking
  tokens; error = danger status token (web text-rose-300).
- Composition: 4 specimen sections (Headings / Body & supporting / Labels & metrics / Inline),
  every role covered exactly once, each rendered in its real role style via the Dynamic-Type-aware
  `TypographyRoleStyle` modifier (@ScaledMetric, anchored to .body).
- States (all render — no hidden surface): loading (redaction skeleton), empty (friendly message),
  error (retry), data (the specimen). Orthogonal connection axis live / stale / offline -> header
  freshness chip + banner with a one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition (P4 leaf contract,
  same framing as AiUsageCard; the source-less web component genuinely has none of these, so they
  are reachable through the P1/S8 source seam and exercised by tests, not fabricated in the
  default path).
- Data binding: bound through `TypographyModel` over the `TypographySource` P1/S8 seam; no HTTP in
  the view. Default `InMemoryTypographySource` emits a fresh, ready catalog.
- i18n (P1/S10): the web source is anonymous (no t()); per the native no-English-literals rule all
  49 strings the surface renders are promoted to the "Typography" table (Typography.strings).
  Swift<->catalog cross-check: 49 keys referenced, 49 defined, 0 missing, 0 unused.
- Accessibility: combined VoiceOver labels on every specimen row + chips, header trait, Dynamic
  Type (ScaledMetric role scaling), reduce-motion honoured (TSFadeIn).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): `view.opened` emitted once on first presentation, surface slug "Typography".

